          "rationale": "The Agreement imposes no most-favoured-nation obligation on the Company. The only economic terms running from us to HDI are the Section 3 fee provisions (30% of Net Sales above $11,000 per month, Sections 3.1–3.3) and the Section 4.2 Termination Payment formula; none requires us to extend HDI terms no less favourable than those given to any third party or to match a third-party offer. The single \"no less favorably\" comparison mechanic (Section 1.8) is an obligation on HDI to promote the Site and Deerskin Products no less favourably than its own catalog titles — an MFN-style benefit running to us, which the playbook expressly welcomes and directs not to be redlined. Section 6.1 exclusivity and the Section 6.1 \"Deerskin\" Marks licence are sourcing/brand-exclusivity terms, not a best-terms or right-to-match mechanic, and belong (if anywhere) under the exclusivity rule rather than being flagged twice here. This therefore sits at the preferred position (no Customer MFN), and no redline is warranted.",
